5
00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:57.900
<v Daniel>No, it is actually a much duller and frankly much more fascinating mechanism. What we are looking at is a side effect of how large language models or LLMs actually work under the hood. These models are fundamentally trained to produce the statistically most</v>

6
00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:12.311
<v Daniel>likely continuation of a sentence, which means by sheer mechanical design, they pull all writing toward the dead Senate of the Bill Kirsch. Nobody plotted this. It is just happening at scale right now. Every single time</v>

7
