<v Daniel>Facebook likes, they genuinely encode highly sensitive private attributes. We're talking about sexual orientation, political views, personality types. Our language is quite literally a biometric fingerprint.</v>

16
00:02:46.759 --> 00:03:01.382
<v Maya>And this is exactly where it gets so tense. Talk about a double edged sword. Because for over a decade, that Kaczynski finding was treated as this massive, terrifying privacy threat. It was the thing we all needed to defend against. The idea that some mega corporation could read my casual tweets and instantly build a</v>

