<v Maya>A social dilemma. I see. Because for me, as an individual, sitting at my laptop clicking improve readability on an email is a totally rational choice. I get a clear benefit. My boss thinks I sound more professional. But collectively, when millions of us make that identical rational choice, the entire</v>

67
00:09:50.992 --> 00:09:58.558
<v Maya>ecosystem becomes identical. And the crazy thing is you can't see that collective cultural loss from inside your own Google Doc. You just think you wrote a great email.</v>

68
00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:09.144
<v Daniel>Precisely. Which naturally pushes us to the next big question the Cerati team asked. If we're all writing a bit more alike, what is the actual measurable cost of that?</v>

