123
00:18:21.117 --> 00:18:35.487
<v Daniel>True, the baseline isn't perfect, but it's the relative drop in their accuracy that tells the story. The AI undeniably makes them worse at their job. So if we pull the thread through all of this, Kaczynski proved back in 2013 that language carries our identity.</v>

124
00:18:36.288 --> 00:18:48.957
<v Daniel>It's our fingerprint. Padma Kumar, Doshi Agarwal, and Wang. They each found a piece of the homogenization effect in a lab, a domain, or a practice, showing how AI pulls us to the center and erases cultural nuance.</v>

125
00:18:49.400 --> 00:19:02.016
<v Maya>And now Serati has proven the immense terrifying scale of this. Hundreds of thousands of real documents starting the very day ChatGPT shipped. It survives every robustness check they threw at it and its cost is not aesthetic.</v>

126
00:19:02.176 --> 00:19:14.871
